<sn><md>### Check silently with `rclone lsjson`

```bash
rclone lsjson mega:Documents/file.pdf
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Use a Bash script

```bash
if rclone lsf mega:Documents/file.pdf | grep -q "file.pdf"; then
    echo "File exists"
else
    echo "File does not exist"
fi
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Check using the exit status

A simpler method:

```bash
if rclone size mega:Documents/file.pdf &gt; /dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1; then
    echo "File exists"
else
    echo "File does not exist"
fi
```

For scripting, checking the command's exit status is usually the most useful approach.
</md></sn>